1. **An optical proximity sensor for locating an object within a detection plane, the optical proximity sensor comprising:**

a plurality of optical sensing pairs arranged at respective positions relative to the detection plane, each optical sensing pair including a light emitter configured to emit light along a respective optical path intersecting the detection plane and a light detector configured to generate a detection signal responsive to light from the respective light emitter that is affected by the object;

drive circuitry configured to activate the light emitters;

readout circuitry configured to receive the detection signals from the light detectors; and

a controller configured to determine a location of the object within the detection plane based on a combination of detection signals generated by at least two of the optical sensing pairs.
